.TH "SUFFIX" "1" "2026\-08\-08" "Suffix 0.1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
suffix \- manage durable short links, domains, photos, and files on
suffix.org
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[CR]suffix [COMMAND] [ARGUMENTS] [OPTIONS]\f[R]
.PP
\f[CR]suffix man [show]\f[R]
.PP
\f[CR]suffix man install [\-d|\-\-dir DIR]\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Suffix is the command\-line client for
\f[CR]https://suffix.org/api/v1\f[R].
It manages shortcuts and domains belonging to a saved account, uses
Somme for configuration and authenticated requests, and supports
multiple local account profiles.
With no command it prints an overview of the active account\(cqs
shortcuts and saved profiles.
.PP
All optional arguments have equivalent short and long forms.
Positional account selectors operate for one invocation without changing
the active profile.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS login
\f[CR]suffix login [EMAIL] [\-u|\-\-app\-url URL] [\-e|\-\-email EMAIL] [\-a|\-\-account NAME] [\-n|\-\-name KEY\-NAME] [\-r|\-\-renew] [\-o|\-\-no\-open] [\-t|\-\-timeout SECONDS]\f[R]
.PP
Select a matching saved account or start browser approval and store a
new API key.
The positional email and \f[CR]\-\-email\f[R] are equivalent and
conflict when both are supplied.
A matching stored key is reused unless \f[CR]\-\-renew\f[R] is present.
\f[CR]\-\-account\f[R] selects the local profile name,
\f[CR]\-\-name\f[R] labels a newly minted dashboard key,
\f[CR]\-\-app\-url\f[R] changes the approval site,
\f[CR]\-\-no\-open\f[R] prints rather than opens the URL, and
\f[CR]\-\-timeout\f[R] defaults to 120 seconds.
.SS logout
\f[CR]suffix logout ACCOUNT\f[R]
.PP
Forget the selected profile\(cqs API key while retaining cached
metadata.
.SS ls
\f[CR]suffix ls [ACCOUNT] [\-j|\-\-json] [\-x|\-\-xml] [\-y|\-\-yaml] [\-l|\-\-stats]\f[R]
.PP
List shortcuts as tab\-separated shortcut and target columns.
\f[CR]\-\-stats\f[R] adds visit counts.
Exactly one structured output flag may be selected.
The hidden compatibility flag \f[CR]\-d|\-\-domains\f[R] lists domains;
prefer \f[CR]suffix domain ls\f[R].
.SS search
\f[CR]suffix search REGEXP [ACCOUNT]\f[R]
.PP
Search shortcut URLs and targets using a case\-insensitive regular
expression.
Output is tab\-separated match scope, shortcut, and target.
.SS add
\f[CR]suffix add [OPTIONS] VALUE [TAIL] [TARGET\-URL] [ACCOUNT]\f[R]
.PP
Create a redirect or Photo shortcut.
\f[CR]VALUE\f[R] may be \f[CR]HOST/TAIL\f[R], a target URL, or a public
tail depending on the selected form.
.PP
Options:
.TP
\f[CR]\-d, \-\-domain HOST\f[R]
Explicit shortcut hostname.
.TP
\f[CR]\-p, \-\-public\f[R]
Use public \f[CR]suf.cx\f[R]; omit a tail for generated candidates or
provide a custom tail before the URL.
.TP
\f[CR]\-l, \-\-letters\f[R]; \f[CR]\-a, \-\-alphanumeric\f[R]; \f[CR]\-w, \-\-words\f[R]
Candidate styles for \f[CR]\-\-public\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-i, \-\-domain\-id ID\f[R]
Domain ID; defaults to the first owned domain.
.TP
\f[CR]\-t, \-\-title TITLE\f[R]
Optional shortcut label.
.TP
\f[CR]\-P, \-\-photo\f[R]
Create a Photo shortcut.
.TP
\f[CR]\-m, \-\-photo\-mode local|remote\f[R]
Stored or original image mode; requires \f[CR]\-\-photo\f[R] and
defaults to remote.
.TP
\f[CR]\-D, \-\-allow\-duplicate\-target\f[R]
Create another shortcut even when the target already has one.
.TP
\f[CR]\-e, \-\-edit\-existing\f[R]
Replace an occupied tail rather than failing.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r, \-\-protect\f[R]
Password\-protect the stored photo; requires \f[CR]\-\-photo\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-f, \-\-password\-file PATH\f[R]
Read the storage password from a file instead of prompting; requires
\f[CR]\-\-photo\f[R].
.SS edit
\f[CR]suffix edit SHORTCUT\-ID [\-t|\-\-tail TAIL] [\-u|\-\-target\-url URL] [\-n|\-\-title TITLE] [\-a|\-\-active BOOL] [\-v|\-\-version VERSION] [ACCOUNT]\f[R]
.PP
Edit selected shortcut fields.
An empty title removes it.
If \f[CR]\-\-version\f[R] is omitted, Suffix reads the current version
before performing the optimistic update.
.SS upload
\f[CR]suffix upload [\-d|\-\-domain HOST] VALUE FILE [ACCOUNT] [\-i|\-\-domain\-id ID] [\-t|\-\-title TITLE] [\-p|\-\-protect] [\-f|\-\-password\-file PATH]\f[R]
.PP
Upload a Business file of up to 100 MB and create a shortcut that
downloads it.
\f[CR]VALUE\f[R] is \f[CR]HOST/TAIL\f[R], or just \f[CR]TAIL\f[R] with
\f[CR]\-\-domain\f[R].
Deleting the shortcut removes its managed object.
.SS rm
\f[CR]suffix rm SHORTCUT\-ID [ACCOUNT] [\-v|\-\-version VERSION]\f[R]
.PP
Delete a shortcut, looking up its version when omitted.
The hidden \f[CR]\-d|\-\-domain\f[R] compatibility flag removes a
domain; prefer \f[CR]suffix domain rm\f[R].
.SS photo
\f[CR]suffix photo SHORTCUT\-ID (\-l|\-\-local|\-r|\-\-remote|\-d|\-\-drop) [ACCOUNT] [\-v|\-\-version VERSION]\f[R]
.PP
Select stored\-image mode, original\-image mode, or remove the managed
image.
Public Photo URLs accept \f[CR]?L\f[R] and \f[CR]?R\f[R] one\-request
overrides.
The three mode flags conflict.
.SS password
\f[CR]suffix password SHORTCUT\-ID (\-a|\-\-add|\-r|\-\-remove) [ACCOUNT] [\-f|\-\-password\-file PATH] [\-v|\-\-version VERSION]\f[R]
.PP
Add, change, or remove password protection on a managed photo or file.
Without \f[CR]\-\-password\-file\f[R], adding prompts without echo.
.SS mv
\f[CR]suffix mv DOMAIN [ACCOUNT] [TARGET] [\-t|\-\-to|\-f|\-\-from] [\-y|\-\-yes] [\-n|\-\-dry\-run]\f[R]
.PP
Move a domain between saved accounts.
The default and \f[CR]\-\-to\f[R] direction move from the active account
to \f[CR]ACCOUNT\f[R]; \f[CR]\-\-from\f[R] reverses it.
Supplying \f[CR]TARGET\f[R] explicitly identifies both source and
destination.
\f[CR]\-\-yes\f[R] skips confirmation.
\f[CR]\-\-dry\-run\f[R] proves both accounts and validates the
recipient\(cqs capacity without changing ownership.
.SS transfer
\f[CR]suffix transfer DOMAIN [\-t|\-\-to EMAIL] [\-m|\-\-minutes MINUTES]\f[R]
.PP
Create a short\-lived domain transfer code.
\f[CR]\-\-to\f[R] restricts acceptance to one email.
Expiration defaults to 15 minutes.
.SS accept
\f[CR]suffix accept CODE\f[R]
.PP
Accept a domain transfer code into the active account.
.SS domain
\f[CR]suffix domain ls [ACCOUNT] [\-j|\-\-json] [\-x|\-\-xml] [\-y|\-\-yaml] [\-l|\-\-stats]\f[R]
.PP
List domains.
Structured formats are mutually exclusive; \f[CR]\-\-stats\f[R] includes
aggregate visits.
.PP
\f[CR]suffix domain add HOSTNAME [ACCOUNT]\f[R]
.PP
Add a domain to the selected account.
.PP
\f[CR]suffix domain rm ID [ACCOUNT]\f[R]
.PP
Remove an empty domain.
.SS account
\f[CR]suffix account [\-l|\-\-long] [\-e|\-\-email EMAIL] [\-k|\-\-key KEY] [\-u|\-\-api\-base URL] [ARGS...]\f[R]
.PP
With no arguments or \f[CR]ls\f[R], list profiles.
A single profile name selects it.
\f[CR]add NAME \-\-key KEY\f[R] stores a profile, with optional email
and API base.
\f[CR]rm NAME\f[R] forgets it.
\f[CR]\-\-long\f[R] includes cached API base, inventory counts, refresh
state, and errors.
The default API base is \f[CR]https://suffix.org/api/v1\f[R].
.SS stats
\f[CR]suffix stats SHORTCUT\-ID [ACCOUNT] [\-d|\-\-days DAYS]\f[R]
.PP
Read aggregate shortcut statistics for a UTC window from 1 through 90
days.
The default is 30.
.SS config
\f[CR]suffix config\f[R]
.PP
Print active API base, selected profile, whether a key exists, and the
configuration path without exposing a secret.
.SS man
\f[CR]suffix man [show]\f[R]
.PP
Print this complete embedded manual.
.PP
\f[CR]suffix man install [\-d|\-\-dir DIR]\f[R]
.PP
Install \f[CR]suffix.1\f[R] using Somme\(cqs shared installer.
Without \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R], standard Homebrew, local, user\-local, and
system section\-1 directories are tried.
.SH COMPATIBILITY COMMANDS
The hidden \f[CR]shortcuts\f[R] and \f[CR]domains\f[R] namespaces
preserve older API\-shaped scripts.
Prefer the public terse commands above.
.TP
\f[CR]suffix shortcuts list\f[R]
List shortcuts.
.TP
\f[CR]suffix shortcuts create \-d|\-\-domain\-id ID \-t|\-\-tail TAIL \-u|\-\-target\-url URL [\-n|\-\-title TITLE] [\-p|\-\-photo] [\-m|\-\-photo\-mode local|remote]\f[R]
Create a shortcut.
.TP
\f[CR]suffix shortcuts update \-i|\-\-id ID \-v|\-\-version VERSION \-d|\-\-domain\-id ID \-t|\-\-tail TAIL \-u|\-\-target\-url URL [\-n|\-\-title TITLE] [\-a|\-\-active BOOL] [\-p|\-\-photo] [\-m|\-\-photo\-mode local|remote]\f[R]
Replace API fields with optimistic concurrency.
.TP
\f[CR]suffix shortcuts delete \-i|\-\-id ID \-v|\-\-version VERSION\f[R]
Delete a shortcut.
.TP
\f[CR]suffix domains list\f[R]
List domains.
.TP
\f[CR]suffix domains add \-n|\-\-hostname HOSTNAME\f[R]
Add a domain.
.TP
\f[CR]suffix domains delete \-i|\-\-id ID\f[R]
Delete a domain.
.SH AUTHENTICATION AND ACCOUNTS
Browser login creates a one\-time API key and returns it through a
loopback callback on \f[CR]127.0.0.1\f[R].
Keys are stored by named profile.
Environment credentials override stored values.
API keys authenticate only their bound account; an administrator key may
bypass product quotas for its own inventory but does not gain
cross\-account authority.
.SH OUTPUT AND RATE LIMITS
Human list output is tab\-separated.
JSON, XML, and YAML are intended for automation.
API failures go to standard error and produce nonzero status.
Suffix consumes Somme\-compatible rate\-limit headers; Free and Pro
exhaustion resets at the next UTC day, while server\-verified
administrators receive an explicit unlimited limit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[CR]SUFFIX_API_BASE\f[R]
Override the saved API base.
.TP
\f[CR]SUFFIX_API_KEY\f[R]
Override the saved bearer key.
.TP
\f[CR]HOSTNAME\f[R], \f[CR]COMPUTERNAME\f[R]
Used in the default dashboard key label.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.suffix\f[R]
Extensible TOML configuration containing named profiles and Suffix
settings.
A sole profile is selected automatically; multiple profiles use the
explicit active account selected by \f[CR]suffix account use\f[R].
Existing platform \f[CR]suffix/config.toml\f[R] configuration is read as
a migration fallback until the next save.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
suffix login person\(atexample.com
suffix add \-d pair.rs typesec https://example.com/type\-security
suffix add \-p \-l https://example.com/public
suffix ls \-l
suffix edit shortcut\-id \-u https://example.com/new \-v 4
suffix photo shortcut\-id \-l
suffix upload \-d pair.rs report ./report.pdf \-p
suffix domain ls \-j
suffix man install \-d \(ti/.local/share/man/man1
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success.
Nonzero indicates parser validation, local I/O, login, authentication,
API, optimistic\-concurrency, quota, transfer, upload, or manual
installation failure.
